<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Vijaynagar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1577 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Vijaynagar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Rajput state in the forested hills of northern Gujarat, also known as Pol, on the borderlands with Rajasthan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The state took its earlier name from Pol, a hill town among the Aravalli spurs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha</a> region. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> rulers held this frontier zone from the later 16th century, though the details of its founding are poorly recorded.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The ruler, styled Rao, governed a sparsely settled tract of hills and forest with a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhil</a> population. In the British period the state was grouped in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha Agency</a>. The area is known for its ruined temples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polo-forest">Polo</a>, deep in the forest near the old capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1948 the state was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a>, and its territory became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabarkantha-district">Sabarkantha district</a> when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> was formed in 1960. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polo-forest">Polo</a> forest is now a protected area.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vijaynagar-state.jpg" alt="Vijaynagar State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Vijaynagar_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1577 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vijaynagar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pol, Vijaynagar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1762&amp;focus=vijaynagar-state" aria-label="Vijaynagar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6625 1308 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vijaynagar State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6945 1564L7364 1601M6945 1564L7364 1602M6945 1564L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6945 1564h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6945 1564h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1762&amp;focus=vijaynagar-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
